    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "A new metallic inserter for the Gravigard IUD was tested on 798 patients. The inserter replaces the old plastic one, it is reusable, and sensibly lowers the price of the device. Insertion proved to be much easier than with the old inserter, especially in cases of retroverted uteri. No expulsions were observed immediately after insertion, but a rate of 1.2%-1.8% of expulsion was noted during the first month. There were 16 cases of pelvic infection, of which 14 were very minor. 2 cases of perforation and 1 pregnancy were reported."
    }
